  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Humanitarian Response to Venezuelan Migrants, Refugees and Vulnerable Populations - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">During the COVID-19 pandemic, IOM worked on improving access to health services and strengthen protection and integration assistance to the migrant and refugee population from Venezuela in Colombia, Ecuador and Peru; while seeking to empower Civil Society; and in Venezuela, to strengthen the capacities of shelter and food security of populations in vulnerable conditions, people returning to Venezuela and those in a situation of pendular migration. This intervention is framed within the RMRP from 2019 to respond to the large-scale population movements recorded in Latin America and the Caribbean due to the political, socioeconomic and human rights situation in Venezuela. Through this action, IOM complements the efforts of the Governments of Colombia, Ecuador and Peru to respond to the flow of refugees and migrants from Venezuela. In addition, this project aims to strengthen inter-agency coordination at the regional level for a more coherent, harmonized, inclusive and representative response of all partners of the Inter-agency Coordination Platform, including Civil Society organizations.</narrative>
  </description>
